========================================================================

| File | Lines | sha256 |
|------|------:|--------|
| `ooda/std/str.oo` | 64 | f276669cd00105e276f0af15ac8b402978652565cdc2b6c1dd538024ce549496 |
| `ooda/std/core/str.oo` | 64 | same (cmp IDENTICAL) |

`grep -i -E 'regex|template|format|split|join'` on **those two files**:
exit=1 both runs. No `regex.oo` / `format.oo` / `template.oo` under
`ooda/std`. Org `std/` has no `str.oo`.

**pub fn names (same 12 in both):**
`str_len` `str_is_empty` `str_eq` `str_contains` `str_concat`
`str_char_at` `str_sub` `starts_with` `ends_with` `index_of`
`repeat` `to_uppercase`

RFC-002 "length / eq / concat / sub only" undercounts 8 wrappers
(`is_empty` `contains` `char_at` `starts_with` `ends_with` `index_of`
`repeat` `to_uppercase`). All similar basics. **Not** reject-class.

False-friends elsewhere (not string APIs): `thr_join` / `join_task`
(thread join); `async.oo` "CAP-G4 split" comment; `semver.oo` says
"no regex engine."

